---
import {
  examplePricing,
  markupComparisonMargin,
  markupComparisonPriceCents,
  marginComparisonMargin,
  marginComparisonPriceCents,
  markupVsMarginDifferenceCents,
  EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT,
} from "../../lib/salesPageExamples";
import { formatCurrency, formatPercent } from "../../lib/calc";
---

<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
  <p class="mx-auto max-w-xl text-center text-lg font-semibold text-ink">
    Adding {EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}% to cost does not create a {EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}% margin.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-center text-base text-muted">
    Example project — true cost <strong class="font-bold text-ink">{formatCurrency(examplePricing.trueCostCents, { cents: true })}</strong>,
    target margin <strong class="font-bold text-ink">{EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}%</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2" data-reveal-group>
    <div class="reveal-item rounded-2xl border border-border bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">{EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}% markup</p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        {formatCurrency(examplePricing.trueCostCents, { cents: true })} × 1.{EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT} = <span class="font-bold text-ink">{formatCurrency(markupComparisonPriceCents, { cents: true })}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">Actual margin: <span class="font-bold text-red">{formatPercent(markupComparisonMargin)}</span></p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-red">Looks like {EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}%. Isn't.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-item rounded-2xl border border-lime-surface bg-mint p-6 shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mint-ink">{EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}% margin</p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
        {formatCurrency(examplePricing.trueCostCents, { cents: true })} ÷ (1 − 0.{EXAMPLE_TARGET_MARGIN_PERCENT}) = <span class="font-bold text-ink">{formatCurrency(marginComparisonPriceCents, { cents: true })}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/80">Actual margin: <span class="font-bold text-mint-ink">{formatPercent(marginComparisonMargin)}</span></p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-mint-ink">Price required to hit the target.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-forest p-6 text-center text-white sm:p-8">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-lime">Difference on this example</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-5xl font-extrabold tabular-nums sm:text-6xl">{formatCurrency(markupVsMarginDifferenceCents, { cents: true })}</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-white/75">
      That's more than five times the $99 lifetime price of Landscape Estimate Pro — in this example alone.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-muted">
    Example only. Your results depend entirely on your own costs, production rates and pricing decisions.
  </p>
</div>
